            <ArticleTitle>[Chase's amputation in a patient with melanoma on the index finger: about a case].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>188</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.11604/pamj.2017.27.188.8512</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We report the case of a 40-year old patient referred by the Depatment of Dermatology at the Ibn Sina Hospital in Rabat for amputation of the index finger as a result of a melanoma diagnosed by biopsy. The amputation was performed according to Chase's method. Aesthetic and functional outcome was very good six months following surgical treatment.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
